      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **Approved** — All checks pass.\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality**: All prior functional issues (circular FIFO wrap-around, multi-byte FIFO read/write indexing, optional `int-gpios` initialization assertion, and active-low interrupt pin deassertion when FIFO interrupts are disabled) are resolved.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: Migrating `emul_lsm6dso` to `i2c_common_emul` and exposing `emul_lsm6dso_append_sample` and `emul_lsm6dso_append_raw_tag` in `zephyr/include/emul/emul_lsm6dso.h` aligns cleanly with the Zephyr I2C emulator architecture and supports both standard sample injection and raw FIFO tag testing in the stacked test CLs.\n* **Code Simplicity**: Watermark status and interrupt pin state updates are centralized in `emul_lsm6dso_set_fifo_count`, `lsm6dso_emul_set_interrupt_pin` computes the pin state without redundant branches, and `emul_lsm6dso_append_sample` selects the sensor-specific parameters in a single branch.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**: Named register masks, shifts, and buffer size macros (`LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS1_DIFF_MASK`, `LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS2_DIFF_MASK`, `LSM6DSO_FIFO_DIFF_MSB_SHIFT`, `LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT`, `LSM6DSO_FIFO_MAX_SAMPLES`, `LSM6DSO_REG_COUNT`) are used consistently throughout.\n* **Security**: Bounds checks in `emul_lsm6dso_append_raw_tag`, `lsm6dso_emul_read_byte`, and `lsm6dso_emul_write_byte` prevent out-of-bounds buffer and register accesses.\n* **Testing**: Exercised by the companion `drivers.lsm6dso` unit test suite in the relation chain (`twister -c -s drivers.lsm6dso`).\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: `Size: L (+306, -73)` (16 added header macro lines in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.h` and 290 added / 73 removed test-emulator lines across `zephyr/emul/`, `zephyr/include/emul/`, and `zephyr/dts/bindings/emul/`). Splitting the `drivers.lsm6dso` test suite into a separate stacked CL keeps this change focused on a single cohesive logical change to the Zephyr emulator.\n*